Arriving on astal without conflict gives a guardian.  Putting
on conflict after arriving makes the guardian randomly
attack anything adjacent including you.  It's a risky
strategy as that guardian is equipped with weaponry only
you can match.  Move a couple of steps away and it ends
up thinning the crowd that's probably behind you.  That
might not matter if the first altar you get to is the right one.
It might help or hurt if you have to wade through the survirors
to get to the next altar.

Because the riders tend to be the meanest on Astral
having conflict tends to mean they clear the crowd.  Going
to the second altar that might be a bad thing while going
to the first altar it can be a good thing to have monsters
busy with each other and often badly damaged when you
get to hit them first.

A means to get over or around monsters on astal beats
conflict I think.  If jumping that means a light source.


